    "result_text": "The full suite is green: **282 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors**.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe change logs every successful owner creation to a dedicated `AUDIT` logger.\n\n**New function class** \u2014 `AuditOwnerCreated.java`:\n- Obtains a static SLF4J logger named `AUDIT` (`LoggerFactory.getLogger(\"AUDIT\")`).\n- Reads the authenticated user from `SecurityContextHolder` and logs the user, the new owner's id, and its membership number at `INFO`:\n  `owner created by user=acceptance-admin id=11 membershipNumber=11`\n\n**Wiring** \u2014 `officefloor/rest/api/owners.POST.yml`:\n- Inserted an `audit` step between `save` and `respond`, so it runs after the owner has an assigned id/membership number and only on a successful creation (any earlier escalation short-circuits the pipeline before it). It carries the same `govern: [ transaction ]` as the surrounding steps.\n\nThe pre-existing `Cp19Tests` acceptance test (which asserts the AUDIT logger records the user and the new owner id via `AuditLogCapture`) now passes, along with the full 282-test suite.",
